Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the configuration system setting all keys in a deprecated key list to the same value without properly treating them as aliases. This meant that when one deprecated key was set, it inadvertently changed the value of all related new keys, causing inconsistency and unexpected behaviors when accessing these configuration values. The enhancements aimed to correct this by ensuring that setting any single deprecated key properly cascades the value change to all its associated aliases, maintaining correct behavior across multiple key mappings.

